# `tsr generate` writes routeTree.gen.ts with LF endings on every build. On a
# Windows checkout git hands the file back with CRLF, so the generator and the
# working copy disagree about a file neither side edited — `npm run build`
# leaves the tree dirty and `git status` shows a modification whose `git diff`
# is empty.
#
# Pinning this one generated file to LF makes the checkout match what the
# generator writes. Deliberately not `* text=auto eol=lf` for the whole repo:
# that fixes the same annoyance but renormalises every file at once, and a
# thousand-line commit touching nothing would bury the history that matters.
src/routeTree.gen.ts text eol=lf
